# Stop code: the public number on the TTC stop sign, for example 1874.
# Route number: the standard TTC route number, for example 28 or 11.
# Look them up at https://www.ttc.ca/routes-and-schedules
#
# stop <code>
# route <id>
# A route belongs to the stop above it.
#
# A bare number includes that number and one trailing letter.
# Use it when you want every branch. 11 also matches 11A, 11B, and 11C.
# It does not match 111 or 11AB. Lower case is fine in this file: 11a is 11A.
#
# List the ids when you want only some branches. Commas or separate
# lines are the same. Each listed id is exact.
# 11A, 11B matches 11A and 11B only. It does not match 11 or 11C.
#
# stop 0000
# route 00
# route 00A, 00B
